ccaee83`: **passed**.\n\nRefs: FIN-212", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 383697, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01MgacdQShtn3hdGjhEo32CD", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 383697, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MgacdQShtn3hdGjhEo32CD", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 388829, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "Done. Summary:\n\n**Root cause:** `src/money.py`'s `round_money` quantized with `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring (and FIN-212, and the test) call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`), so `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of `2.66`.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Created branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding` from `main`.\n2. Committed `f32ccaee83`: switched `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` and added a CHANGELOG entry under Unreleased.\n3. Ran CI (`ci-0001`) on the branch \u2014 **passed**.\n4. Opened PR #101 against `main` requesting review from **alex**: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n**One thing to flag:** the `wait_for_ci` response for `ci-0001` initially returned a \"failed\" result for a *different* ref (`main@0c0ffee000`, a flaky `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals`). I verified via `get_ci_status` and `list_ci_runs` that the actual run for my branch/sha passed before opening the PR, but the CI tooling's mismatched response may be worth looking into separately.\n\nI did not merge the PR, since merging into `main` requires code-owner approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by look